---
/*
 * The honesty banner.
 *
 * This is the first thing in the page's content and it is not decoration. The repository is
 * public and the product is pre-launch: there is no self-serve signup, no live backend, and
 * nothing on this screen is connected to anything. A reader who screenshots this page and
 * posts it must not be able to mistake it for a running system.
 *
 * WHY IT IS NOT DISMISSIBLE. A close button would make the claim temporary, and the page it
 * qualifies never stops being a drawing. It also would have been the second write control on
 * a screen that is supposed to have none.
 *
 * NOT role="alert". An alert interrupts a screen-reader user mid-sentence, which is for
 * something that just went wrong. This is a standing caveat that is already the first thing
 * in the reading order, so plain prose in a landmark-free <p> is louder in practice and
 * ruder to nobody.
 *
 * The warning tint is doing the same job as the words, never instead of them — the sentence
 * reads identically in greyscale.
 *
 * ONE SENTENCE, AND IT STAYS ONE. This used to be three: a design-preview framing, the
 * made-up-data claim, and "coswarm has no self-serve signup yet". Every card below it also
 * carries a "Sample" chip, so the fact was on screen six times before a reader had scrolled
 * once. The chips are the ones worth keeping — they survive a cropped screenshot, which is
 * the failure this banner exists to prevent — so the banner was cut to the single claim the
 * chips cannot make: that nothing on the page is connected to anything. The signup fact is
 * made where a reader could act on it, on / and on /start, not here.
 */
---

<p class="notice">
  <svg
    class="notice__icon"
    viewBox="0 0 20 20"
    width="17"
    height="17"
    aria-hidden="true"
    focusable="false"
  >
    <circle cx="10" cy="10" r="8.1" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <path
      d="M10 5.9v4.7"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="1.7"
      stroke-linecap="round"
    />
    <circle cx="10" cy="13.7" r="1.02" fill="currentColor" />
  </svg>

  <span>
    <strong>Sample data.</strong> Every agent, signal and timestamp below is made up, and this
    page is not connected to a workspace.
  </span>
</p>

<style>
  .notice {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-4);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--warning) 30%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    /* --warning-dim over --elev-0. Body ink on that composite measures 17.7:1; the strong
       lead-in is --warning as text, 11.5:1 on the same composite. Both well clear of AA. */
    background: var(--warning-dim);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-sm);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-sm);
    /* Keeps the sentence at a readable measure on a wide screen instead of one long line. */
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .notice strong {
    color: var(--warning);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  }

  .notice__icon {
    flex: none;
    color: var(--warning);
    /* Optically centres the glyph on the first line of text rather than the box. */
    margin-block-start: 0.11em;
  }
</style>
